  "interchange_note": "An initial bitwise B-rep equality assertion failed on a rational trim coefficient by one ULP. The final round-trip check preserves exact surfaces, topology, component tolerances, and p-curve rational weights and knots; bounds normalized p-curve coefficient changes by 1e-14 and compares lifted geometry at 1e-8. The read-side ordinary continuous boundary checks also run.",
  "limitations": [
    "Matching the exact curved Automatic command-domain policy remains unfinished; geometric preservation is checked separately from the two literal domain failures.",
    "Viewport face picking, block-instance copies, multi-face batch editing and continuous global Rhino parity are not claimed.",
    "SDK-only reference operation: replay is in the command tests, not a new Rust oracle protocol enum variant.",
    "Curved FilletSrf Extend=Yes retains its prior endpoint-policy restriction; no fillet construction or extension algorithm changed.",
    "No C++/FFI implementation changed; no new ASan or general performance claim."
  ],
